// SYNTHETIC — written by hand against packages/protocol/src/schemas/sidecar.ts, not captured from
// a running sidecar. No machine in this project can capture a Dota 2 window: macOS is the only
// platform with a backend and it has never been executed (ADR-0033), and the one backend that runs
// here — `--backend replay` — has no atlas and emits nothing but region digests. So the *hero
// sightings* below are the shape a minimap detector is specified to produce, not the shape one was
// observed to produce. What a real recording would settle: the confidence distribution of template
// matches, how often a hero is missed for a pass or two while still on screen, and whether
// icon-to-position error is small enough for the world-unit conversion in
// `apps/desktop/src/main/sidecar/protocol-codec.ts` to be worth the two decimal places it implies.
//
// One VisionStep per line, and each `event` is a literal SidecarEvent — the same bytes the Rust
// sidecar writes. Deliberately not a compressed notation: a fixture that has to be expanded by a
// function in this repo keeps agreeing with us after the protocol changes underneath it.
//
// The story it tells, which is the vision → coaching edge in miniature:
//   0–400 ms   all five enemies on the minimap, crystal_maiden below the 0.5 confidence gate
//   600 ms     nevermore and tidehunter stop being reported — no message says so, they are simply
//              absent, and ageing is what turns that into `enemy_missing`
//   1000 ms    a pass that recognised nothing: the digest alone, which is what a quiet minimap is
//   1400 ms    exclusive fullscreen, reported rather than absorbed (dota2 §9)
//   1600 ms    a line on stderr, which is not protocol and must not be parsed as any
//   2000 ms    a panic, so the supervisor's restart-with-backoff path has something to restart
